    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: global `customerCode` assignment\n\nNew owners get a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of the last name, a hyphen, and a 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`). It's assigned once at registration and persisted, so it stays stable on later reads.\n\n## Files touched, and why each\n\n- **`service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`** (new) \u2014 a small component with a single responsibility: produce the code for an owner. It owns both the sequence source (`ownerRepository.count() + 1`) and the `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` format. Kept out of the `ClinicServiceImpl` facade so that class doesn't accumulate formatting logic.\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 `saveOwner` now delegates to the generator, but only for a brand-new owner without a code (`owner.isNew() && getCustomerCode() == null`), so updates never regenerate it. Injected the generator via the constructor.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`repository/OwnerRepository.java`** + **`jdbc`/`jpa` impls** \u2014 added `count()`. Spring Data JPA (the active profile) derives it automatically; the other two implementations got explicit `COUNT` queries so everything compiles.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a read-only string on the `Owner` response schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, which MapStruct auto-maps by name \u2014 no mapper change needed. It's absent from `OwnerFields` (the input), so it can't be client-supplied.\n- **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to each owners table (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreFormatAndGlobalSequence`) verifies the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two owners' sequence numbers are consecutive \u2014 both pass, and the full suite is green.",
